-#
  The install progress dialog, shown immediately after `inst/install` returns.

  The job streams into two targets inside the body:
    #install-log     -- appended to as output arrives
    #install-status  -- replaced when the job reaches a terminal state

  `turbo_stream_from` subscribes this dialog to the job's stream. It is inside the modal body
  rather than the layout because the subscription is only wanted while this dialog is open;
  when it is dismissed the element is removed and the client unsubscribes.

  `close_button: false` suppresses the modal's own footer button so the footer's Close is the
  single documented way out. Close always goes to the app's show page, whether or not the job
  has finished; the job continues in the background either way.

= turbo_stream.update("modal-frame") do
  = v.modal(t("app_installs.progress_title"), size: "lg", close_button: false) do |modal|
    = turbo_stream_from AppInstallJob.stream_name(@install.job_id)

    %dl.row.small.mb-3
      %dt.col-4.col-md-3.text-muted= t("apps.name")
      %dd.col-8.col-md-9= @install.instance_id
      %dt.col-4.col-md-3.text-muted= t("jobs.state_label")
      %dd.col-8.col-md-9
        = render "app_installs/status", outcome: :running, message: nil

    -#
      The pane the job appends to. It starts with a prompt so an empty log does not read as a
      broken feed; the first appended chunk will not remove it (append, not replace), so it
      simply scrolls out of view.
    %pre.mb-3.install-log{id: "install-log"}
      .text-muted= t("app_installs.awaiting_output")

    .btn-toolbar
      = v.link_button(label: t("app_installs.close"), icon: "arrow-right",
                      url: app_path(@install.instance_id), color: "primary", fill: true)
